   "evidence": "Line 20 is `types: [synchronize, labeled]`. The merge job filter at lines 66-67 accepts every `synchronize` event, and accepts `labeled` only when the label is `ready-to-merge`. The `workflow_run` filter at line 70 still requires `event == 'pull_request_target'`, so dispatched builds never trigger this workflow directly.",
   "file": ".github/workflows/auto-merge.yml",
   "fix": "Describe each event on its own, e.g. '# synchronize: a pushed head is immediately unsafe until it has current-head reviews. labeled (ready-to-merge only): pr-status reconciliation, including after dispatched maintenance builds, marked the PR ready.'",
   "issue": "The new comment 'Recheck pushed heads and newly ready PRs after dispatched maintenance builds.' ties `synchronize` to dispatched maintenance builds. `synchronize` fires on any push, whether or not a maintenance build ran. The edit also deletes the old reason for the trigger: a pushed head is unsafe until it has current-head reviews. Dispatched builds reach this workflow only indirectly: pr-status adds the `ready-to-merge` label, and that `labeled` event triggers this workflow.",
   "line": 18
  }
 ],
